{
  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "source": "Power BI semantic model (Import mode)",
    "grain": "one row per ticket line sold",
    "model": "star schema — 1 fact, 5 conformed dimensions"
  },
  "legend": [
    { "id": "lg-fact", "kind": "entity", "label": "Fact table (grain: one ticket line sold)", "color": "#1d4ed8" },
    { "id": "lg-dim", "kind": "entity", "label": "Dimension table", "color": "#cbd5e1" }
  ],
  "edgeDirectionSets": [
    {
      "id": "s-card",
      "name": "Cardinality (1 to *)",
      "style": { "stroke": "#475569", "lineStyle": "solid", "startMarker": "crowsFootMany", "endMarker": "crowsFootOne" }
    },
    {
      "id": "s-filter",
      "name": "Filter direction",
      "style": { "stroke": "#7c3aed", "lineStyle": "dashed", "startMarker": "none", "endMarker": "arrowClosed" }
    }
  ],
  "activeEdgeDirectionSetId": "s-card",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "blurb",
      "type": "text",
      "position": { "x": -470, "y": -620 },
      "size": { "width": 1240, "height": 300 },
      "style": { "fill": "#fefcbf", "fillOpacity": 92, "stroke": "#d69e2e", "fontColor": "#744210", "fontSize": 12, "textAlign": "start", "fontFamily": "sans-serif" },
      "data": {
        "label": "EXAMPLE — Power BI star schema: Meridian Rail ticket-sales model\n\nIllustrates: a data architect / BI developer laying out a Power BI semantic model — one fact table, five conformed dimensions. Uses multi-line labels for table columns, crow's-foot markers for cardinality, and EDGE DIRECTION SETS for the two ways a Power BI relationship reads:\n  • \"Cardinality (1 to *)\"  — the FK->PK structure: many fact rows to one dimension row.\n  • \"Filter direction\"      — how filter context propagates at query time: dimension -> fact (single-directional).\nSame five relationships, opposite arrows. Switch between the readings in Diagram settings -> Edge direction sets; the legend row follows the switch.\n\nPersona: a data architect on Meridian Rail's modernization task force, designing the reporting model over the new booking platform.\n\nPart of the Meridian Rail example gallery — epic 0022 (docs/planning/epics/0022-example-diagram-gallery.md)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fact_ticket_sales",
      "type": "entity",
      "position": { "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "size": { "width": 300, "height": 262 },
      "style": { "fill": "#1d4ed8", "stroke": "#1e3a8a", "strokeWidth": 2, "fontColor": "#ffffff", "fontSize": 12, "textAlign": "start", "fontFamily": "monospace" },
      "connectionPoints": [
        { "id": "cp-bl", "side": "bottom", "offset": 0.28 },
        { "id": "cp-br", "side": "bottom", "offset": 0.72 }
      ],
      "data": {
        "label": "Fact Ticket Sales\n─────────────────────\nDateKey  (FK)\nRouteKey  (FK)\nOriginStationKey  (FK)\nPassengerKey  (FK)\nChannelKey  (FK)\n· · · · · · · · · · · · ·\nQuantity\nGrossFare\nDiscountAmount\nNetRevenue",
        "details": "star-schema-powerbi/details/fact-ticket-sales.md"
      }
    },
